日期: 2025-08-20

1
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:22,160
《星际迷航: 新世界》前情提要
Previously on Star Trek: Strange New Worlds...

2
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:23,650
史波克 这是詹姆斯·柯克
Spock, meet James Kirk,

3
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,020
法拉格特号的大副
first officer of the Farragut.

4
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:26,160
当年我刚接受任命时
When I took my commission,

5
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:27,260
跟着派克学习了一周
I spent a week shadowing Pike.

6
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,060
那段经历让我受益匪浅
It made all the difference.

7
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,700
你知道几乎永生
You want to know the worst thing

8
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:33,030
这件事最糟糕的一点是什么吗
about living almost forever?

9
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:34,470
你会失去你爱的人
The loss of those you love.

10
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,080
这不是你的错 克里斯
It wasn't your fault, Chris.

11
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:37,470
我是领队人
I led the mission.

12
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:39,070
我们得对别人的生命负责
We're responsible for other people's lives.

13
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:41,670
船员们的性命就是我的一切
The lives of my crew mean everything to me.

14
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:44,380
我们的职业让我们不得不频繁的面对死亡
Our job puts us up against death

15
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:45,450
这本就不公平
more than is fair.

16
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,750
你可以选择让死亡赢过你
Now, you can let death win

17
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:50,080
又或是挺身反击它
or you can fight back.

18
00:00:56,790 --> 00:01:00,090
大副私人日志 星历
First officer's personal log. Stardate...

19
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:02,830
星历到底是怎么算的
What is the stardate?

20
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,660
日子全都混淆在一起了
They're all blending together.

21
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:07,700
法拉格特号正在联邦星域外
Farragut is conducting a planetary survey

22
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,600
对一颗无人居住的M级星球 赫利孔γ星
of Helicon Gamma, an uninhabited M-class world

23
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:12,800
进行行星勘测
outside Federation space, and...

24
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:19,110
而我实在是无聊极了
...I am so deeply bored.

25
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:22,780
我发现最近总是忍不住质疑
I find myself constantly questioning

26
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:24,390
维瑞尔舰长的命令
Captain V'Rel's orders.

27
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:27,020
对于风险 她避之唯恐不及
It's like she's allergic to risk.

28
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:29,090
我们在宇宙里是要干实事的
We're out here to get our hands dirty,

29
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:31,040
是来探索的
to be explorers,

30
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,530
而不是对着扫描数据三重核查 纸上谈兵
not to triple-check every sensor reading.

31
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,580
我明白
I get it.

32
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,440
她想严格按照规定来办事
She wants to do everything by the book.

33
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:39,930
昨天晚上到现在有什么变化吗
Any changes since last night?

34
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:41,760
我只是觉得如果规定是我定的
I just think the book would be more interesting

35
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,170
事情会变得更有趣一些
if I got to write it.

36
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:44,540
舵手
Helm,

37
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,180
带我们去北部大陆上空的
bring us into a low geosynchronous orbit

38
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:47,960
近地同步轨道
over the northern continent.

39
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:51,310
维瑞尔舰长
Captain V'Rel, if I may,

40
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,560
如果我们能再靠近一点的话
we could get much more detailed readings

41
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,180
就能得到更多更具体的数据了
from an even lower orbit.

42
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:57,400
你说的是多近
How low do you suggest?

43
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,280
最近的那种
Lowest orbit there is.

44
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:00,460
亲自踏上星球的土地
Our boots on the ground.

45
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:02,720
考虑到地质不稳定的因素
Given the geological instability,

46
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,460
这样做会带来不必要的风险
it seems an unwarranted risk.

47
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,900
我们来就是为了风险的 不是吗
Risk is why we're here, isn't it?

48
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:08,590
不然星际舰队只要发一颗探测器过来就好了
Starfleet could have sent a probe,

49
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:10,060
但是他们让我们来了
but instead they sent us

50
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:12,330
因为有些事必须要我们亲眼所见
because some things you need to see for yourself

51
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,170
-才能真正理解 -舰长
- to truly understand. - Captain,

52
00:02:14,270 --> 00:02:15,640
刚刚有一股未知的力量撞到了
an unknown force just impacted

53
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:17,140
赫利孔γ星的地表
Helicon Gamma's surface.

54
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:18,020
报告
Report.

55
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:20,110
检测到行星地壳发生地震波扰动
There's a seismic disturbance in the planet's crust.

56
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:26,040
红色警报
Red alert.

57
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,960
舵手 规避机动
Helm, take evasive action.

58
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,750
全体船员 做好冲击准备
All hands, brace for...

59
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,060
医疗团队马上到舰桥
Medical team to the bridge.

60
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,660
这里是联邦星舰法拉格特号
This is the USS Farragut.

61
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,020
我们需要紧急援助 我们遭受严重损伤
We need immediate assistance. We've taken heavy...

62
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,140
长官 有什么东西在干扰我们的通讯信号
Sir, something's interfering with the comms signal.

63
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,900
我正在尝试识别其来源
I'm trying to identify the source.

64
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:31,110
是那玩意发出的干扰
It's coming from that.

65
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,100
读数怎样
Readings?

66
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,230
还有生命信号
Life signs on board,

67
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:44,120
但我们的人手只够操作星舰的
but barely enough to crew the ship.

68
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:45,980
这么多系统宕机
Multiple systems nonfunctioning.

69
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:48,380
看在贝尔德的份上到底怎么回事
What in Baird's name happened here?

70
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,180
看在谁份上?
Whose name?

71
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,850
那个苏格兰籍的发明家
The Scottish inventor.

72
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:53,420
无人不知约翰·罗杰·贝尔德啊
Everyone knows John Logie Baird.

73
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:00,620
救援来了吗
Rescue?

74
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:01,480
我们的确是来救援的
That is our purpose.

75
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:03,180
问题是 谁袭击了你们
The question is: rescue from what?

76
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:06,020
我只看见了一眼 特别大的东西
I only saw a glimpse. It was huge.

77
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,380
他正在内出血
He's got internal bleeding.

78
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:09,280
我需要把他带到医务室去
I need to get him to sickbay.

79
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,400
我最好赶紧去轮机室
I'd better go to Engineering

80
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:11,910
去看看曲速核心怎么样了
and check there's still a warp core.

81
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,110
之后来汇报你们的发现
Report back with your findings.

82
00:06:13,210 --> 00:06:14,250
我们会在舰桥
We will offer our assistance

83
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,710
帮助维瑞尔舰长
to Captain V'Rel on the bridge.

84
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:17,820
等等
Wait.

85
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:18,880
不光是舰对舰通讯
It's not just ship to ship.

86
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,310
所有的通讯都不能用了
All comms are down.

87
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:21,960
我们没法和彼此保持联系
We'll have no way to get in touch with each other.

88
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:22,640
去吧 
Go. 

89
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,280
但到时候在尽快在舰桥汇合
But find your way to the bridge as soon as you can.

90
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:30,420
你给我好好撑住
Don't you shut down on me.

91
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:32,320
增援到了
Reinforcements have arrived.

92
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:36,660
你们的首席医疗官呢 少尉
Where's your CMO, Ensign?

93
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:41,860
好吧 只剩你了
Just you, then.

94
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:44,910
身上好多都是钝器伤
I'm seeing a lot of blunt-force injuries in here.

95
00:06:44,910 --> 00:06:45,680
发生了什么
What happened?

96
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,000
你应该去问舰长
You should ask the captain.

97
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,270
她在四号床
Bed four.

98
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:53,080
维瑞尔舰长 我是查普尔护士
Captain V'Rel, I'm Nurse Chapel.

99
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:58,090
你有些脑挫伤 但没有颅脑肿胀
You have a cerebral contusion. There's no cranial swelling.

100
00:06:58,090 --> 00:06:59,550
我需要回舰桥去
I need to get back to the bridge.

101
00:06:59,550 --> 00:07:01,590
嗯 等我们确定了
Mm-hmm, right after we make sure

102
00:07:01,590 --> 00:07:03,160
你没有脑疝的症状之后再说
that your brain isn't herniating.

103
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,400
躺下
Stay.

104
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,700
我们的外勤队已经去舰桥了
Our away team is heading to the bridge.

105
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:08,970
他们会帮忙的
They can help.

106
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:13,360
试试绕过主传感器系统
Try bypassing primary sensors.

107
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,270
检查侧向阵列还有没有未损坏的功能模块
See if anything's functioning in the lateral array.

108
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,570
阿尔瓦雷斯 带我们离开这片残骸区
Alvarez, get us out of this debris.

109
00:07:18,570 --> 00:07:21,220
长官 没有传感器的话太危险了
Sir, it's too dangerous without the sensors.

110
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,240
-舰长 -维瑞尔舰长把指挥权交给了我
- Captain... - Captain V'Rel left me the conn,

111
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:25,200
我的职责是确保船的安全
and it's up to me to return it intact.

112
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,400
史波克先生
Mr. Spock.

113
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:30,820
乌乎拉少尉 拉安
Ensign Uhura. La'An.

114
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:31,780
欢迎登舰
Welcome aboard.

115
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:32,320
詹姆斯
James.

116
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,900
你这边的乱子真是有够大的
Quite a mess you've gotten yourself into.

117
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,290
看起来这是我的专长
Seems to be my specialty.

118
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:37,620
你们能接到求救信号真是奇迹
It's a miracle you got our distress call.

119
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:38,540
通讯都被干扰了
Signal was jammed.

120
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,320
信号干扰也对我们造成了严重的影响
The interference has wreaked havoc with us, too.

121
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:42,030
但我也许能建立一条视讯连接
But I might be able to set up line of sight.

122
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,460
请求借用你们的遥测仪器
Permission to borrow your telemetry?

123
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:44,480
完全可以
More than granted.

124
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,810
阿尔瓦雷斯 让我们靠近进取号
Alvarez, aim us at the Enterprise.

125
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,390
准备联系舰长
Stand by for the captain.

126
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,610
派克舰长
Captain Pike.

127
00:08:00,610 --> 00:08:02,120
鉴于目前情况十分危急
I'll dispense with the pleasantries

128
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,650
我就不多说客套话了
since we're still in a critical situation.

129
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,160
威胁目标还在当前区域吗
Is the threat still in the area?

130
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,020
我不清楚
Unknown.

131
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:07,590
告诉我你知道的信息
Tell me what you do know.

132
00:08:07,590 --> 00:08:10,780
我们当时正在对赫利孔γ星进行地质勘测
We were in the middle of a geological survey of Helicon Gamma 

133
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,060
就在这时
when--

134
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:13,800
坦白说 实在无法用科学术语来描述当时的状况
well, there's no scientific way to put it--

135
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,980
星球瞬间天崩地裂
all hell broke loose.

136
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,620
-因为星球不稳定吗 -不是
- Planetary instability? - No.

137
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,620
一束聚焦的引力束瞄准了这颗行星
A focused gravitational beam aimed at the planet.

138
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,200
被什么瞄准的
Aimed by what?

139
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,100
拥有发射功率如此强大的牵引光束
A ship capable of generating a tractor beam that 

140
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,170
这飞船的规模恐怕
powerful would have to be...

141
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:26,860
比有记录以来的任何星舰
Several orders of magnitude bigger

142
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,210
都要大上好几个数量级
than any starship on record.

143
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:31,580
我知道这听起来很荒谬 但这是真的
I know. It sounds crazy, but it's true.

144
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:34,420
我们差点都没发现它 它对我们不感兴趣
We barely saw it. It wasn't interested in us.

145
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:35,940
我们不过是它的连带损伤
We were just collateral damage.

146
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,280
灭世者
Destroyer of Worlds.

147
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,640
然后它就消失了吗
And it just disappeared?

148
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,340
我们撞上碎片的时候 传感器
When the debris hit, we lost sensors,

149
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:42,060
通讯 所有重要系统都损坏了
comms, all critical systems.

150
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,860
维瑞尔舰长虽已受伤 但意识尚清
Captain V'Rel was injured but lucid enough

151
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:45,900
足以下达撤离指令
to give the evacuation order.

152
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,380
逃生舱已部署完毕
Escape pods have been deployed.

153
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,160
我会留下最低限度的留守人员
I'm keeping a skeleton crew aboard

154
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,920
尽量避免法拉格特号沦为需要打捞的废船
so Farragut doesn't become a salvage job.

155
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,820
你做得很好
Well, you've performed commendably,

156
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:55,240
但还是把你们都一并救出来吧
but let's get you all to safety.

157
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,570
一号 让法拉格特号的全体成员
Number One, I want all Farragut crew

158
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:57,740
立刻传送到舰上来
beamed aboard immediately.

159
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:58,370
明白 舰长
Aye, Captain.

160
00:08:58,370 --> 00:08:59,870
全员撤退 从逃生舱开始
Full evacuation. We'll start with the escape pods.

161
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:01,180
执行吧
Proceed.

162
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:01,700
派克舰长
Captain Pike...

163
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,960
我明白 我也不会放弃我的星舰
I know, I wouldn't want to give up my ship either,

164
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,000
但舰员的安全必须放在首位
but the safety of the crew has to come first.

165
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,350
这是正确的决定
It's the right call.

166
00:09:07,350 --> 00:09:09,240
我们有严重受伤的患者在医务室
We have some critically injured patients in sickbay

167
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,020
缺少医生照顾
and no doctor.

168
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:10,660
乌乎拉少尉
Ensign Uhura,

169
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:12,860
跟查普尔确认哪些患者需要紧急撤离
confirm with Chapel which patients require immediate evac 

170
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:13,760
然后把他们送往进取号
and get them to Enterprise.

171
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:14,400
马上去办 舰长
On it, Captain.

172
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,590
在你撤离之前
Before you evacuate,

173
00:09:15,590 --> 00:09:17,840
把该未知星舰的所有战术信息传输给进取号
transfer all tactical info on this mystery ship.

174
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,420
以防他们再次出手 我要做好充足的准备
I want to be ready if they take another swing.

175
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:21,100
我已经恢复了部分传感器的功能
I have restored some function to sensors.

176
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,420
我们仅有的这点数据就交给
Sending what little data we have back

177
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:23,390
努尼恩·辛格上尉带回
with Lieutenant Noonien-Singh.

178
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,880
我现在就传送回舰 舰长
Beaming back now, Captain.

179
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,300
我来亲自把这个交给你
I'll hand this to you personally.

180
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,440
开始传送
Energize.

181
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,270
现在 把你们全部的系统
Now put all your systems...

182
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,980
乌乎拉 重新接通
Uhura, get him back.

183
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:33,940
发生什么了
What happened?

184
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,340
恐怕连不上了
I don't think I can.

185
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:39,260
为什么
Why not?

186
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,640
阿尔瓦雷斯 我需要你负责战术岗位
Alvarez, I need you on tactical.

187
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,660
准备好所有武器
Prepare all weapons.

188
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:50,800
明白 长官
Aye, Commander.

189
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,990
进取号在视野内 他们正在交战
We have visual on Enterprise. They are engaging.

190
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:03,480
用上所有的武器朝对方开火
Whatever we've got, fire at that thing.

191
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,710
这不合逻辑
That is illogical.

192
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:06,340
进取号的武器明显起不到任何作用
Enterprise's weapons were clearly ineffective.

193
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,610
我们的瞄准系统下线了
Our targeting systems are down.

194
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,310
现在开火的话作用极微
Firing would serve little purpose

195
00:10:09,410 --> 00:10:10,380
-并且还有可能会误伤进取号 -那我们总得做点什么吧
- and risk damaging Enterprise. - Well, we have to do something.

196
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:11,300
那我们总得做点什么吧
- and risk damaging Enterprise. - Well, we have to do something.

197
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,340
我们不能坐着干等着
We can't just sit here.

198
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:20,460
此刻
At present,

199
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,920
恐怕我们只能这么做
I am afraid that is all we can do.

200
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:39,640
诊断 我现在就要完整的舰船诊断报告
Diagnostic. I want a complete ship diagnostic right now.

201
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:42,400
这里有一些好消息
Uh, well, here's some good news.

202
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,540
我们不再受到干扰了
We're not being jammed anymore.

203
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:44,540
好的
Great.

204
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:46,320
舰桥呼叫医务室 
Bridge to sickbay. 

205
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,400
我需要尽快和维瑞尔舰长通话
I need to speak to Captain V'Rel ASAP.

206
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,620
查普尔护士回报
Nurse Chapel reporting.

207
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:51,150
她需要进行紧急颅骨切除术
She required an emergency craniectomy,

208
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,620
而我没有能力实施这个手术
which I'm not qualified to perform,

209
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,090
于是两分钟前
so I beamed her to the Enterprise

210
00:10:54,090 --> 00:10:55,790
我已将她传送至进取号
two minutes ago.

211
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,500
指挥官 你现在是法拉格特号的舰长了
Commander, you are now captain of the Farragut.

212
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,400
我们静候您的命令 长官
We await your orders, sir.

213
00:11:25,730 --> 00:11:27,990
有什么你能辨别出来的吗
Anything you recognize?

214
00:11:27,990 --> 00:11:29,790
可能是克林贡的 难说
Klingon maybe. Hard to say.

215
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,820
这里没剩下多少东西能去辨别了
There's not much left to recognize.

216
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:33,790
有些看起来年头还不小
Some of them seem ancient.

217
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,400
损伤报告如何
Damage report.

218
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,630
主动力离线 所有网络系统都失效了
Main power's off-line, all network systems are down.

219
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:39,840
引擎 武器 内部通讯系统
Engines, weapons, internal comms.

220
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,400
便携式通讯器还是不能用
Hand communicators still are not working.

221
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,230
太多干扰了
Too much interference.

222
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,380
维生系统呢
Life support?

223
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:44,460
在以最低限度工作
Working but minimal.

224
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:45,480
派一名通讯员去
Send a runner.

225
00:11:45,570 --> 00:11:47,310
口头通知舰员到星舰中部空间集中
Tell the crew to gather in central spaces.

226
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:49,450
舰体外壳附近的区域会冷死人的
Areas near the outer hull are gonna get pretty damn cold.

227
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:52,680
舰长 我们派遣到轮机部的通讯员一直没回来
Captain, the last runner we sent to Engineering hasn't come back.

228
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:54,880
那只能假设我们已经被登舰了
Then we have to assume that we've been boarded.

229
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,900
法拉格特号的传感器日志有什么信息
Did the Farragut's sensor logs tell us anything

230
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:58,180
能看出建造这艘船的种族吗
about the species that built this thing?

231
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,280
他们的船体对于我们的传感器来说几乎不可穿透
Their hull is nearly impenetrable to our sensors,

232
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,660
但看得出来他们的科技极为先进
but it's clear they're incredibly advanced.

233
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,890
舰长 你听说过阿萨斯里克吗
Sir, have you heard of Asaasllich,

234
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,330
灭世者
Destroyer of Worlds?

235
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:08,320
它还有一个译法是噬星者
It-it also translates as Astrovore.

236
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,780
噬星者吗 没听过
Astrovore? No.

237
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:11,480
每个在偏僻的殖民地长大的孩子
Well, every child growing up

238
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,570
都听说过它
on a remote colony world has.

239
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,670
不同的名字 但本质上是一个东西
Different names, same story.

240
00:12:15,670 --> 00:12:18,280
一艘有数百年历史的拾荒船
Scavenger ship, hundreds of years old,

241
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,740
在已知星域的边缘之外游弋
prowling just beyond the edges of known space.

242
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,010
从各种行星以及
Consuming resources from planets

243
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:23,850
所有不幸与其相遇的舰船身上掠夺资源
and any ship unlucky enough to cross its path.

244
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,940
我在边境附近任职时也听过一个说法
I heard a version when I was posted near the border.

245
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:29,520
克林贡人称其为查克-卡 意为湮灭者
Klingons called it Chach-Ka. "The Annihilator."

246
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:31,320
索耶上将也在他的星际制图课上
Admiral Sawyer told a story like that

247
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,880
讲过类似的故事
in his Stellar Cartography class.

248
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:34,740
地图边缘之外的怪物
The monster past the edge of the map.

249
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,380
无论是不是那艘传说中的飞船
Whether or not this is that ship,

250
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:37,780
我们已经确定它是一艘拾荒船
we know it's a scavenger.

251
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:39,220
我们必须假设他们
We have to assume that their intention

252
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,980
也打算把进取号给撕碎
is to tear the Enterprise apart as well.

253
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,560
一号 我需要你和奥特加斯合作
Number One, I need you and Ortegas to find a way

254
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,200
找到重新让引擎上线的方法
to get engine control back online

255
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,560
这样只要我们赶去轮机室
so that when we get to Engineering

256
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,900
一旦阻止能量流失
and we stop the power drain,

257
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,870
我们就能逃跑了
we're ready to make a run for it.

258
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,080
代理舰长日志
Acting captain's log.

259
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:58,150
这个称谓读着很奇怪
Feels strange to say that.

260
00:12:58,540 --> 00:13:01,200
要不是事态这么糟糕 我应该会很兴奋吧
Under better circumstances, it would be thrilling.

261
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,520
我已经让进取号的军官们
I've asked the Enterprise officers to fill in

262
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:06,340
去各自填补舰桥上的岗位空缺
for our missing bridge crew.

263
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,290
但他们几乎不了解我
But they barely know me,

264
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:09,790
而现在我却要他们完全信任我
and now I have to ask them to trust me.

265
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,860
如果我是他们的话
If I were in their shoes...

266
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:16,960
暂停记录 请进
Pause recording. Come in.

267
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,620
柯克舰长 我们整理了所有
Captain Kirk, we compiled all of the data

268
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:21,760
与外星飞船遭遇时获取的数据
from our encounter with the alien vessel.

269
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,570
我们都知道些什么
What do we know?

270
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:25,500
我们的传感器无法彻底穿透其船壳
Our sensors cannot fully penetrate its hull,

271
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,320
因此 关于飞船的构成
so we can ascertain little of its composition,

272
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,680
性能或船员配置 我们基本都无法确定
capabilities or crew complement.

273
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:29,910
它的弱点呢
What about weaknesses?

274
00:13:29,910 --> 00:13:31,580
根据基础数学知识 按照它的尺寸
Fundamental math? Its size.

275
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:34,140
对于这么大的家伙来说
It would be hard to generate a stable warp field

276
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:35,210
要维持稳定的曲速场是很难的 对吗
at that scale, wouldn't it?

277
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:36,720
这么说 它应该会很慢
Well, odds are, it's slow, but...

278
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,020
那我们就能抓到它
But then we can catch it.

279
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,000
按照规定
Regulations...

280
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,180
按照规定 我们本该夹着尾巴
Regulations would have us tuck tail

281
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:42,860
逃回联邦星域
and run back to Federation space.

282
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,780
等我们连上子空间通讯中继
By the time we reach a subspace relay

283
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:45,660
搬到援兵的时候
and get reinforcements,

284
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,500
进取号早被拆成碎片了
Enterprise will have been ripped to scraps.

285
00:13:53,630 --> 00:13:55,670
我们都有亲友在
We all have people on...

286
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:58,600
我哥哥在那艘船上
My brother is on that ship.

287
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,640
您是最高级的军官 我们都将服从您的命令
As the ranking officer, we will follow your orders.

288
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:03,600
我只是想为您提供所有的相关信息
I merely wished to provide you with all relevant information.

289
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:05,510
这些信号是尼斯湖水怪嘴里那些
Those are the signatures

290
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:07,800
被拆解的外星飞船所留下的
from the picked-apart alien ships we saw in Nessie's gob.

291
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,040
把那里放大点看 得吗
Enhance that bit, would you?

292
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:17,520
其中的一艘是克林贡D7级战巡
One of the vessels is a D7-class Klingon cruiser.

293
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:18,730
里面可能有幸存者吗
Could any of them have survived?

294
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:20,220
极其不可能
Highly unlikely.

295
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:21,820
船体装甲板将会被拆解
The hull plating would be disassembled,

296
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:22,880
所有可呼吸空气都会泄漏出去
venting all breathable air.

297
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,840
即便是克林贡人都不能杀出一条血路
Even the Klingons couldn't fight their way out.

298
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,880
这些拾荒者 他们从舰船上拿走中意的东西
These scavengers, they take what they please from ships--

299
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,300
不管舰员的死活 还要把这些技术篡改后据为己有
damn the crew-- and pervert the tech into their own.

300
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,570
我们没法估量他们到底有多大能耐
We've no idea what they're capable of.

301
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:33,180
查普尔说得对
Chapel's right.

302
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,800
如果速度就是我们的武器 那好钢必须用在刀刃上
If speed is our weapon, then we have to press it.

303
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:35,860
什么速度
What speed?

304
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:37,910
恕我直言 指挥官
Uh, with all due respect, Commander--

305
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:40,480
还是 代理舰长
I mean, Acting Captain?

306
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,800
还是就是舰长
Is it just Captain? Uh...

307
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,750
长官 他们本可以轻松摧毁法拉格特号
Sir, they easily could've destroyed the Farragut

308
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:47,760
或是把我们塞进那该死的巨大囊袋里掳走
or made off with us tucked in their bloody huge pouch,

309
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,640
但他们没有这么做
but they didn't.

310
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:49,880
你心里对此有什么推论吗
And you have a theory as to why?

311
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:52,300
可能因为你的星舰受损太严重了
Because your ship's so banged up

312
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,660
不值得他们去偷吧
it wasn't worth stealing?

313
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,900
那我需要你变出个奇迹了 斯考特先生
Well, then I need you to perform some miracles, Mr. Scott.

314
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,900
按顺序 我们先弄引擎 再弄武器
We need engines and weapons, in that order.

315
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:00,620
明白
Aye.

316
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:01,380
把损伤修理好
Patch up the wounded.

317
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:02,500
尽快让它们重新上线
Get them back to work as soon as you can.

318
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,500
我们得弄清楚
We need to figure out where

319
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,830
那艘拾荒船要驶向哪里
that scavenger ship is headed

320
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,080
这样才能设法快他们一步
so we can find a way to get there first.

321
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:08,870
就这样吧 让我们开工
That's it. Let's get going.

322
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:23,260
真是怀念涡轮电梯啊
Really missing the turbolift.

323
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:25,430
没事 就剩八层甲板两条梯子要爬了
Only eight decks and two access ladders left to go.

324
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,570
哦不 别开枪
Oh! Oh, no, don't shoot.

325
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:36,260
人活了五千年可不是为了挨枪子的
You don't live to be 5,000 by getting yourself shot a lot.

326
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:37,470
我们正在前往轮机舱的路上
We're on our way to Engineering.

327
00:15:37,470 --> 00:15:39,840
这可不兴去了 除非你想
Bad place to be right now unless you're fond

328
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:44,150
被自己汩汩涌出的鲜血呛死
of choking to death on your own gurgling blood.

329
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,710
怎么会这样
Wh... From what?

330
00:15:45,810 --> 00:15:47,650
都怪那条脐带
The umbilical!

331
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:49,820
跟着我 来
Come with me. Come.

332
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:52,380
那里弥漫着有毒气体
It's flooded with toxic gas.

333
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:55,360
它直接穿透了我们的船体
It's tunneled straight through our hull.

334
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,420
它已经接入了我们的动力系统
It's tapped into our power systems,

335
00:15:57,420 --> 00:16:00,360
计算机网络和燃料贮箱
our computer network, our fuel storage.

336
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:04,040
我们连辅助动力都没剩多少
We've barely any auxiliary power left.

337
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,540
如果我们不想法把它断掉
If we don't disconnect it,

338
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:07,140
就没有足够的动力来逃脱了
we will not have enough to escape.

339
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:08,820
既然空气是有毒的 我们需要戴上呼吸器
If the air is toxic, we'll need breathers

340
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:10,100
才能接近脐带
to get close to the umbilical.

341
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:12,520
拿上东西 米勒少尉会护卫你们的队伍
Grab them. Ensign Miller will escort your team.

342
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:13,740
我们摆脱了那东西的那一刻
The second we disconnect from that thing,

343
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:15,340
就要马上准备好逃离
we need to be ready to fly.

344
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:16,780
是 舰长
Yes, Captain.

345
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,780
对 给我听着
Yeah, you heard right.

346
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:27,440
你最好给我管用 你这小破玩意
You better start doing your job, you daft piece of...

347
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,340
斯科特先生
Mr. Scott?

348
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:29,540
一切进展顺利吗
Everything okay in there?

349
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:33,160
会的会的 只要我先拆几个东西出来
Soon will be, once I've torn a few things out

350
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,540
然后再把它们装回去
and put them back proper.

351
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,300
然后 这需要多久
An-And how long will that take?

352
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,760
正常的做法吗 两天
To do it right? Two days.

353
00:16:38,870 --> 00:16:40,270
唔
Hmm.

354
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:42,900
要不你先这样 先确保
Why don't you start with doing it the way

355
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,800
我们不会立即散架爆炸
where we won't immediately explode,

356
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:46,220
然后再在此基础上做点别的
and we'll take it from there?

357
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,260
史波克和乌乎拉有突破了
Spock and Uhura made a breakthrough.

358
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,120
哦 是吗 哎哟
Oh, aye? Oh.

359
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,710
这艘拾荒船在赫利孔γ星
The mineral that the scavenger ship was collecting

360
00:16:52,710 --> 00:16:54,910
收集的矿物是奥登金
at Helicon Gamma-- it was aldentium.

361
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:56,350
哦我听过
Oh, I've heard of it.

362
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:59,500
有几个种族把它用在推进系统上
A few species use it in their... propulsion systems.

363
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:02,280
附近还有另一颗拥有大量矿藏的行星
There's another world nearby with significant deposits--

364
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,800
沙利文星 就在他们的路线上
Sullivan's Planet-- directly in their path.

365
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:07,700
有人居住吗
Inhabited?

366
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,930
超过一亿人口
Over a hundred million people.

367
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:12,200
而且是曲速前文明 所以还有不干涉原则
Pre-warp, so the non-interference directive

368
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,800
意味着我们不能直接警告他们
means we can't warn them.

369
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:15,470
不过我们也没别的手段做些什么
Not that there's anything we could do anyway.

370
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:17,580
但听着 我们一定要比他们先到那里
Listen, we need to get there first.

371
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:19,300
给拾荒船设个埋伏
Set a trap for the scavengers.

372
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:21,670
你不会是觉得 在他们抢跑了这么久之后
You're not asking me to warp us past them,

373
00:17:21,770 --> 00:17:23,170
我还能让咱们赶到他们前头去吧
with the head start they've got?

374
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:24,980
这样 恢复曲速动力我没问题
Look, I can give us warp power,

375
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:27,040
但如果你觉得这东西
but if you think this tub will hold together

376
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:30,490
都被砸成这样了 在高曲速下还能不散架
at high speed after the beating she just took,

377
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:32,220
还是少做白日梦了
your bum's out the window.

378
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:34,490
等离子导管都
The plasma manifolds...

379
00:17:34,490 --> 00:17:35,760
我理解
I understand.

380
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:37,300
我不觉得你理解
No, I'm not sure you do.

381
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:38,860
你拿到了个烂摊子 对吧
You were handed a raw deal, all right?

382
00:17:38,990 --> 00:17:40,360
没人会指责你搞砸了什么
No one can fault you for that.

383
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:43,430
但如果我们把这艘船推得太猛 把她弄散架了
But if we push this ship too hard and it fails,

384
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,700
那就是我们的问题了
that's our fault, not theirs.

385
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,470
这是风险
It's a risk.

386
00:17:47,530 --> 00:17:49,700
但我把赌注压在我们自己身上
But I am betting on us.

387
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,380
准备进入最高曲速
Prepare for maximum warp.

388
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,600
怎么了
What's the problem?

389
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,890
我刚刚绕开了所有安全措施
I just bypassed every safety feature

390
00:18:06,890 --> 00:18:09,590
建立了与舰舵控制的直接连接
to make a direct connection to the helm controls.

391
00:18:10,430 --> 00:18:12,100
我本该立即被电得魂飞魄散的
I should've shocked the bejesus out of myself.

392
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:14,180
没把自己炸得灰头土脸你还失望了吗
Disappointed you didn't set your hair on fire?

393
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,530
如果剩余的电力连让我触电都做不到
If there's not enough power to do that,

394
00:18:15,530 --> 00:18:17,800
那就更不够驱动星舰转向了
there's nowhere near enough to steer the ship.

395
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,370
这声音是好迹象吗
That's a good sound, right?

396
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:22,460
这船不会叫得很开心吧
The ship is happy screaming?

397
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:24,240
是提醒我们动作要快点了
It's a reminder to work faster.

398
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,340
我们能人工点火推力器吗
Can we fire the thrusters manually?

399
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:30,980
呃 如果我们想死得痛快的话 可以
I mean, we can if we want to very quickly die.

400
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:33,600
机动推力器使用化学反应点火
The maneuvering thrusters use a chemical reaction.

401
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,050
它们可以手动触发
They can be triggered by hand.

402
00:18:35,050 --> 00:18:37,680
但没有通讯 我们就无法协调推力器的工作
But with no comms, we'd have no way to coordinate them.

403
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:40,480
没有传感器 我们就只能完全盲飞
With no sensors, we'd be flying literally blind.

404
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,520
为什么要传感器 我们可以自己看
Who needs sensors? We have eyes.

405
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,420
别忘了也没有护盾和偏导仪
Add to that no shields or navigational deflector.

406
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:46,360
只要我们犯点错误
If we make a mistake,

407
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:47,620
而且这个情况下肯定会
which we definitely would,

408
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:49,140
我们就要变成舱壁上的一团黑炭了
we end up a scorch mark on the wall.

409
00:18:49,140 --> 00:18:50,840
通讯问题吗
Communication issue?

410
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,820
那我来得正好
I got here just in time, then.

411
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:55,200
这可能是第一次
This may be the first time I'm glad

412
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:58,870
我庆幸自己在1980年代生活过
to have lived through the 1980s.

413
00:19:00,510 --> 00:19:01,910
舰长
Captain.

414
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:07,440
它直接连在了我们的电网上
It is hooked directly into our power grid,

415
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:09,480
我们的计算机系统上 还有燃料吊舱上
our computer systems, and our fuel pods.

416
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,660
可以尝试用相位枪切断它
We could try to sever it with our phasers.

417
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,180
释放出的能量会炸掉半艘船的
That much energy would take out half the ship.

418
00:19:15,090 --> 00:19:16,460
找掩护
Cover!

419
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,750
我不觉得他们能透过烟雾看清我们
I don't think they can see us through the smoke.

420
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:41,020
快把她带出去
Let's get her out of here.

421
00:19:47,750 --> 00:19:49,790
乌乎拉 情况报告
Uhura, status.

422
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:51,760
接近曲速七级 舰长
Approaching warp seven, sir.

423
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,560
行吧 虽然这船现在基本是拿胶带粘起来的
Well, Farragut may be held together by duct tape

424
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:59,800
但只要没散架就行
at this point, but as long as it holds...

425
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,370
传感器显示我们已经超越拾荒船了
Sensors indicate we have overtaken the scavenger vessel.

426
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,840
干得不错 各位
Excellent work, everyone.

427
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:08,000
我们还有多久抵达沙利文星
How long until we reach Sullivan's Planet?

428
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,540
两个小时 如果能保持当前速度的话
Two hours, if we can maintain this speed.

429
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,980
如果之前有任何人跟我说 这是不可能的
I will be accepting drinks in the galley

430
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:18,920
一会都得来餐厅请我几杯酒
from everyone who said that this was impossible.

431
00:20:20,710 --> 00:20:24,320
当然 是在我们把你们的船救出来之后
After we have saved your ship, of course.

432
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,520
当然
Of course.

433
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:57,260
报告
Report.

434
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:58,780
我们掉出了曲速
Well, we've dropped out of warp,

435
00:20:58,780 --> 00:21:00,360
并且失去了所有引擎动力
and I've lost all engine power.

436
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,620
舰长 按照计划 现在我们
Captain, our stratagem has put us

437
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:02,760
直接位于拾荒船前方的路径上
directly in the path of the scavenger vessel.

438
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:04,230
我很清楚 史波克
I am aware, Spock.

439
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:05,560
我跟你说过的 等离子导管全炸开花了
It's the plasma manifolds-- they've blown out.

440
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:06,700
那就想尽一切办法
Well, then take whoever you need

441
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:08,140
用你能用的一切资源和人力去修
and get down there and fix them.

442
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,400
它们直接炸没了 没法修了
They are gone! Beyond repair!

443
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:10,700
我们现在得进船坞
We'll need to put into spacedock now

444
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:12,070
才能更换它们了
and replace them.

445
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:16,110
我们 我们把她推得太猛了
We just... we pushed her too hard.

446
00:21:16,110 --> 00:21:18,050
现在只能坐以待毙了
We're dead in the water.

447
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:27,580
我告诉过你了 我检查过读数了
I told you, I rechecked the numbers

448
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:29,820
而且检查了三次 三次都告诉我
and re-rechecked them, and all three times confirmed

449
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:32,390
现在曲速引擎就是个超大号镇纸 什么用也不顶了
the warp engines are now giant paperweights.

450
00:21:32,390 --> 00:21:33,990
我们还有一部分脉冲动力
We still have some impulse power.

451
00:21:33,990 --> 00:21:35,190
但也不够
Not nearly enough.

452
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:37,800
我看我们能做的就是装死
I'm afraid all we can do is play dead

453
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:40,100
希望拾荒船能再次忽略我们
and hope the scavenger ignores us.

454
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:42,440
有可能他们还是只打算去快乐地吞掉行星
There's a chance it'll just go on its merry planet-eating way.

455
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:45,880
我们的另一个选项是弃舰并使用穿梭机撤离
Our other option is to abandon ship and escape by shuttle.

456
00:21:46,310 --> 00:21:48,380
我们可以派一架穿梭机到最近的子空间通讯中继
We could take one to the nearest subspace relay

457
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:49,180
然后呼叫星际舰队
and hail Starfleet.

458
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,080
等我们到的时候
By the time we get there,

459
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,760
沙利文星上的所有人早就死透了
everyone on Sullivan's Planet will be dead.

460
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:53,710
结论就是 两个选择都很灾难
So we're agreed, both options are terrible,

461
00:21:53,710 --> 00:21:56,060
但我们总得选一个 一个小时后他们就到那了
but we have to pick one. In one hour it'll be here.

462
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:59,740
我们只有一个小时来决定哪个更不灾难一些
That's how long we've got to decide which is least terrible.

463
00:21:59,740 --> 00:22:01,500
这也不是我们能决定的
That is not our decision to make.

464
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:07,360
我哪个都不选
I pick neither option.

465
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:12,440
好吧 那很勇敢了 而且 如果你不介意我这么说的话
Okay. That is a bold and-- if you don't mind me saying--

466
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:14,200
简直离谱到家了
highly unorthodox choice.

467
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:15,400
行了
Okay.

468
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:16,940
长官 他只是很担心
Sir, he's just concerned.

469
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,720
他们还扣着我们的人
They have our crew,

470
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:21,000
而且正在前往一颗有人居住的行星
and the planet they're headed for is inhabited.

471
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,170
我们无法警告他们 除非
We won't be able to warn them without...

472
00:22:22,270 --> 00:22:23,740
谢谢你 乌乎拉少尉
Thank you, Ensign Uhura.

473
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,750
我对情况很清楚
I'm up to speed on the particulars.

474
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:27,450
没有进一步解释的必要
No need for further discussion.

475
00:22:27,450 --> 00:22:29,360
那我们怎么给你选项呢
Then how will we provide you with options?

476
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:31,320
我不需要选项
I don't need options.

477
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,520
我不需要你们喋喋不休
I don't need chattering voices.

478
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:35,420
我现在需要清空头脑
What I need is to clear my head.

479
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:37,020
但我现在没办法
And I can't do it with all this...

480
00:22:44,530 --> 00:22:46,800
好吧 情况本来可以更好的
Well, that could have gone better.

481
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:48,400
不可能 怎么可能
No. How?

482
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,660
这是他第一次坐舰长椅 是吧
This is his first time in the chair, right?

483
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,040
他以前也接管过指挥 但从来没像这样
He's had the conn before but never like this.

484
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:56,610
他表现出典型的受胁迫下的紧张迹象
He's showing classic signs of strain under duress.

485
00:22:56,710 --> 00:22:57,810
他感受到的压力肯定很
The pressure he must be feeling...

486
00:22:57,910 --> 00:22:59,650
啊 太棒了 起初他还无所顾忌
Aye, great. First he's reckless,

487
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:01,920
现在他又要跟树枝一样一折就断了
now he's liable to snap like a twig.

488
00:23:02,050 --> 00:23:04,020
假设他真断了 那怎么样 嗯
Let's say he does. What then, huh?

489
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:07,120
我们就要采取措施来
We would take steps to...

490
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:09,060
解除他的指挥权
remove him from command.

491
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:12,360
那 那些措施具体是什么
And... what would those steps be, exactly?

492
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:14,500
作为舰上当前最高级别的医疗军官
As ranking medical officer on board,

493
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:16,860
我有权评估他的健康状况
it's within my power to evaluate him

494
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:19,900
并在他在心理上不适合的情况下 解除他的职务
and, if he is mentally unfit, remove him from duty.

495
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:23,170
好吧 在我们考虑这条路之前
Okay, before we even think about going down this road,

496
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:24,670
我们应该先考虑
we should consider

497
00:23:24,770 --> 00:23:26,510
他还能工作 这只是他的风格
that he's still working on his command style.

498
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:29,610
对啊 现在他的风格是装死
Aye. Right now his style is lacking.

499
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,350
这就是问题
That's my point.

500
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:32,810
我们或许可以帮助他找到方法
Maybe we can help him find it.

501
00:23:32,950 --> 00:23:34,990
我以前见过他处理危机
I've seen him in a crisis before,

502
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,150
他没有被迫当舰长的压力的时候
when he didn't have the pressures of being captain.

503
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:41,750
他能看到连我都想不到的自己的潜力
He saw something in me that I hadn't seen in myself.

504
00:23:41,850 --> 00:23:43,490
这救了我的命
It saved my life.

505
00:23:44,930 --> 00:23:46,260
我觉得他只是需要有人提醒
I think he just needs to be reminded

506
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:48,260
他身上也有这种潜力
that same thing is in him.

507
00:23:48,330 --> 00:23:50,130
那我们中就有人需要和他谈谈
Well, one of us should talk to him.

508
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,840
他很显然很激动
He is clearly agitated.

509
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:54,130
或许风格更冷静的人
Perhaps someone with a less emotional style

510
00:23:54,130 --> 00:23:56,000
去和他谈 会更有效果
might be more effective.

511
00:24:06,810 --> 00:24:08,550
莫雷尔 撑住
Maurer... come on.

512
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:10,020
莫雷尔 清醒点
Maurer, stay with us.

513
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:11,760
来不及了  必须现在治疗她
She can't wait. We have to treat her now.

514
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:13,250
现在 那两个家伙还在外面晃荡呢
What, with those two things roaming around?

515
00:24:13,350 --> 00:24:14,620
别无选择了
We have no choice.

516
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:24,030
没法对他们造成任何伤害
They're not taking any damage.

517
00:24:24,030 --> 00:24:26,570
进这里 左舷餐厅
In here, the Port Galley.

518
00:24:31,780 --> 00:24:33,320
没有毒气 安全了
No fumes. We're safe.

519
00:24:37,640 --> 00:24:38,680
她在大出血
She's bleeding out.

520
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:40,040
我需要医疗箱
I need a medkit.

521
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:41,480
等一下 我觉得
Wait, wait, wait, I think...

522
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:49,080
要是我们有通讯器和能用的传送器
If we had comms and a functioning transporter,

523
00:24:49,080 --> 00:24:50,220
是能救她的
we could have saved her.

524
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:52,360
未必 那些离子粒子
You don't know. Those ion particles

525
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,260
就像子弹一样 能撕裂皮肉和骨骼
are like bullets. They rip through flesh and bone,

526
00:24:54,260 --> 00:24:55,490
虽然原始 但杀伤力十足
primitive but effective.

527
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:09,240
可他们的防护服却异常先进
And yet their suits are highly advanced.

528
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:11,300
我从没见过能吸收相位枪火力的设备
I have never seen a device absorb phaser fire like that.

529
00:25:11,300 --> 00:25:12,620
这不合常理
It doesn't make sense.

530
00:25:12,620 --> 00:25:13,380
或许他们来自
Maybe they're from some

531
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:15,420
宇宙中某个永远无法用常理解释的阴暗角落
dark corner of the cosmos that'll never make sense.

532
00:25:15,420 --> 00:25:17,220
我们得想办法解决他们的护甲防御
We have to find a way to get through their defenses somehow.

533
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:21,220
没人见过他们 但我知道
No one has ever seen them, but I know

534
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:23,790
即便是戈恩人 也把他们视作怪物
they were considered monsters, even by the Gorn.

535
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:25,790
相位枪调至击杀模式
Set phasers to kill.

536
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:48,280
这可是我从伊塞奈特酿酒厂进口的酒
I had this imported from an Ithenite distillery.

537
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:50,790
我会赔你一瓶的
I'll get you another one.

538
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:19,950
就像我的一位老朋友曾经说的
As an old friend of mine once said,

539
00:26:19,950 --> 00:26:22,050
「要有光」
"Let there be light."

540
00:26:24,020 --> 00:26:25,450
快点进来吧
Come, come, come.

541
00:26:25,450 --> 00:26:27,820
她的舱室
Her quarters are...

542
00:26:27,820 --> 00:26:30,390
和我想象中的一模一样
exactly what I expected.

543
00:26:32,630 --> 00:26:35,500
在这 不对 好了
Here. No, no. Okay.

544
00:26:35,590 --> 00:26:37,160
在这里
There you are.

545
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:38,770
不是你
Not you.

546
00:26:38,830 --> 00:26:40,400
你以前倒是活泼
You were once bouncy

547
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:42,470
又开朗 可新鲜劲一过
and cheerful, but when the novelty wore off,

548
00:26:42,570 --> 00:26:44,270
就有点吓人了
you got a little creepy.

549
00:26:44,370 --> 00:26:45,540
这些破烂玩意儿
How is any of this junk

550
00:26:45,670 --> 00:26:47,140
怎么帮我们飞离这里啊
going to help us fly out of here?

551
00:26:47,210 --> 00:26:48,610
我的老天
Oh, my goodness,

552
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:51,880
我以前就靠这个操控过不少星舰呢
I piloted many a starship with this.

553
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:54,480
虽然是8比特的船嘛
Granted, they were 8-bit,

554
00:26:54,550 --> 00:26:57,020
但周五晚上玩这个还挺有意思的
but it was a good time on a Friday night.

555
00:26:58,180 --> 00:26:59,150
啊 找到了
Ah, found it.

556
00:26:59,220 --> 00:27:00,760
拿着
Take.

557
00:27:00,850 --> 00:27:03,850
这该不会是
Is this a, uh,

558
00:27:03,960 --> 00:27:05,860
个人按摩器吧
personal massager?

559
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:10,030
哦 这在以前可是最先进的通讯器
Oh, this was once a state-of-the-art communicator.

560
00:27:10,130 --> 00:27:11,830
得插在墙上才能用
You had to plug it into the wall,

561
00:27:11,930 --> 00:27:15,800
不过要是有人烦你 你就能让他们一直等着
but if people annoyed you, you'd put them on hold.

562
00:27:15,900 --> 00:27:17,570
应该还有更多的
I think there are more.

563
00:27:17,670 --> 00:27:19,870
所以信号是通过有线传输的
So the signals are grounded,

564
00:27:19,970 --> 00:27:22,110
从一根线缆直接传到另一根线缆
transmitted cable to cable.

565
00:27:22,210 --> 00:27:23,480
拿着那个
Take that.

566
00:27:23,580 --> 00:27:27,280
这样就能防止信号被干扰了
Which will insulate them from being jammed.

567
00:27:27,380 --> 00:27:28,550
我们要让船员们
We're going to have the crew

568
00:27:28,650 --> 00:27:31,050
拆除船上所有的铜缆
strip the ship for copper cables,

569
00:27:31,150 --> 00:27:34,720
然后给进取号重新布线
and we're going to wire the Enterprise.

570
00:27:39,530 --> 00:27:41,400
快去吧
Go on.

571
00:27:56,110 --> 00:27:58,410
我和维瑞尔舰长之前有一局棋没下完
Captain V'Rel and I had an ongoing game.

572
00:27:58,540 --> 00:28:00,080
那是我第一次觉得
For the first time, I think I was

573
00:28:00,180 --> 00:28:01,450
自己快要赢她了
on my way to beating her,

574
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:03,180
可我们始终没机会结束那局
but we never had the chance to finish.

575
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:04,780
我记得当时棋盘就摆成这样
I think this is how we left the board.

576
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:06,010
恕我打扰
If I may interrupt.

577
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:07,620
哦 你已经打扰了
Oh, you already have.

578
00:28:08,450 --> 00:28:09,920
别停
Don't stop now.

579
00:28:10,020 --> 00:28:11,860
你否决了两个有缺陷的方案
You rightly dismissed two flawed courses of action,

580
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:13,800
但时间紧迫 我们需要新计划
but time is short and we require a new plan.

581
00:28:13,930 --> 00:28:17,730
轮到维瑞尔走棋 我已经把她逼入绝境了
It was V'Rel's move, and I had her in a corner.

582
00:28:18,770 --> 00:28:21,310
要是能想到她接下来会怎么走就好了
If I could just figure out what she would have done next.

583
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:23,440
你现在是代理舰长 船员们都在等你
You are acting captain. Your crew is waiting.

584
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:25,610
让他们等太久对事态
To keep them waiting longer would be...

585
00:28:26,470 --> 00:28:27,780
没有好处
...not good.

586
00:28:27,780 --> 00:28:29,090
问题是
Here's the thing.

587
00:28:32,510 --> 00:28:33,780
我慌了神
I'm frozen.

588
00:28:33,780 --> 00:28:34,910
这倒让我有点意外
I find this surprising.

589
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,120
你哥哥常说
Your brother speaks often

590
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:37,960
你一直想要指挥星舰
of your aspirations for command

591
00:28:38,050 --> 00:28:39,720
也很有领导才能
and of your affinity for leadership.

592
00:28:39,820 --> 00:28:41,120
其实他原话是
Actually, he said

593
00:28:41,220 --> 00:28:42,350
你不管面对谁
you are not afraid to throw your weight around,

594
00:28:42,450 --> 00:28:43,490
都敢直言发令 毫不含糊
no matter who's in front of you.

595
00:28:43,590 --> 00:28:45,360
是啊 这倒像山姆会说的话
Yeah, that sounds like Sam.

596
00:28:48,510 --> 00:28:49,740
某种程度上 他说得没错
And in a way he's right.

597
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:51,330
从我加入星舰学院那天起
From the moment I joined the Academy,

598
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:53,300
我就下定决心要比任何人都快地
I was determined to sit in that chair

599
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:55,900
坐上那把舰长椅
faster than anyone before me

600
00:28:55,900 --> 00:28:58,070
因为我觉得自己比别人更懂行
because I thought I knew better.

601
00:28:58,070 --> 00:28:59,600
觉得自己比别人更优秀
I thought I was better.

602
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,560
每当我觉得命令不合理时
Whenever orders don't make sense to me,

603
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:03,340
而且我总是觉得不合理
which happens more often than I'd like,

604
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:07,840
我总想 该由我来下达命令才对
I always think that I should be the one giving them.

605
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:11,480
之前 我让维雷尔舰长派一支登陆小队
Earlier, I told Captain V'Rel to send a landing party

606
00:29:11,480 --> 00:29:12,820
去赫利孔γ星
to Helicon Gamma.

607
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,820
我当时极力劝说她
I pushed her hard on it.

608
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:20,490
还好她没听我的
Thank God she ignored me,

609
00:29:20,490 --> 00:29:23,620
不然爆炸时 我们只能在地表等死
otherwise we'd all be standing on the surface when it exploded.

610
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,270
优秀的舰长知道该何时倾听
Good leaders know when to listen

611
00:29:26,270 --> 00:29:27,270
何时坚持己见
and when not to.

612
00:29:29,660 --> 00:29:31,140
而我连这一点也没做到
Well, I failed at that test, too.

613
00:29:31,140 --> 00:29:33,180
斯科特先生也警告过我
Mr. Scott warned me

614
00:29:33,180 --> 00:29:34,440
不要强行启动引擎
not to push the engines,

615
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:35,880
可我还是命令他这么做了
but I ordered him to anyway.

616
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:38,720
我这段时间一直凭直觉行事
I've been flying by the seat of my pants this whole time,

617
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:39,880
一次次做决定
making call after call

618
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:42,450
却完全不知道这些决定会带我们走向何方
with no clue where they'd lead us,

619
00:29:42,450 --> 00:29:43,950
只能指望自己碰巧选对
hoping I'd luck into the right one,

620
00:29:43,950 --> 00:29:46,320
结果却让我们困在这
and all I did was put us belly up in the path of

621
00:29:46,320 --> 00:29:47,850
直面那个什么终极毁灭者
the ultimate destroyer.

622
00:29:47,850 --> 00:29:49,760
现在你确实陷入了信心危机
And now you are having a crisis of confidence,

623
00:29:50,460 --> 00:29:51,760
但你还是得继续领导大家
but you still have to lead.

624
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:53,380
说真的 我也想啊
Believe me, I'd love to,

625
00:29:53,380 --> 00:29:55,260
可我现在完全没头绪
but there's nothing coming to me.

626
00:29:59,530 --> 00:30:02,700
我妈妈常说一句话
My mom was fond of an expression.

627
00:30:04,380 --> 00:30:06,840
「实现目标的人 往往不知道接下来该怎么办」
"The dog who caught the car."

628
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:11,950
如今我终于有了机会
Now that I've finally latched onto one...

629
00:30:14,050 --> 00:30:16,850
却不知道该怎么应对
...I have no idea what to do with it.

630
00:30:17,620 --> 00:30:21,290
在瓦肯星 我们也有一句类似的话
On Vulcan, we have a similar expression.

631
00:30:22,190 --> 00:30:24,730
「咬到自己尾巴的赛拉兽」
"The sehlat who ate its tail."

632
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:26,560
不过我要指出 你比那种
Though I would point out you have

633
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:28,960
四足野兽有更多的优势
a significant leg up over a quadrupedal beast.

634
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,630
你的人类直觉
Your human intuition.

635
00:30:30,630 --> 00:30:33,780
它一直指引着我们 我们现在还都好好活着
It has guided us this far. We are all still here.

636
00:30:33,780 --> 00:30:35,330
我建议你继续相信它
I recommend you keep following it.

637
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:42,760
好的
Okay.

638
00:30:43,780 --> 00:30:45,620
既然你这么说
If you insist.

639
00:30:47,960 --> 00:30:50,660
斯科提 那艘拾荒船还有多久到
Scotty, how long until that scavenger ship gets here?

640
00:30:50,660 --> 00:30:53,700
不到 20 分钟 但这只是估算
Less than 20 minutes, but that's just an estimate.

641
00:30:53,700 --> 00:30:54,890
对我来说够了
Well, it's good enough for me.

642
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:57,260
很高兴看到你回来了 长官
Glad to see you back, sir.

643
00:30:57,840 --> 00:30:59,230
我也是
Me, too.

644
00:30:59,230 --> 00:31:02,640
我知道我们开局不顺
Look, I know we got off to a rough start here,

645
00:31:02,640 --> 00:31:05,480
我说什么也弥补不了这一点
and there's nothing I can say that can make up for that.

646
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:08,100
而且激昂的演讲也不是我的强项
Rousing speeches aren't exactly my forte.

647
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:09,440
长官 我觉得你说得很好
I think you're doing just fine, sir.

648
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:13,410
但我要跟在座各位说清楚
But let me be crystal clear to each of you.

649
00:31:13,410 --> 00:31:15,660
即便我之前的行为让你们有别的想法
Even if my actions indicated otherwise,

650
00:31:15,660 --> 00:31:19,420
我也绝不会放弃营救进取号
I have no intention of giving up on rescuing the Enterprise,

651
00:31:19,420 --> 00:31:21,720
毕竟我们两队船员的生命都危在旦夕
not with the lives of both of our crews on the line.

652
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:23,800
谢谢您 长官 我正需要听到这句话
Thank you, sir. I needed to hear that.

653
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:25,100
我也需要听听你们的想法
And I need to hear from you.

654
00:31:25,900 --> 00:31:27,060
我们现在掌握了什么情况
What do we know?

655
00:31:27,060 --> 00:31:29,020
除了我们困在太空中动弹不得之外
Besides the fact that we're dead in space,

656
00:31:29,020 --> 00:31:31,400
关于这些拾荒者 我们还知道什么
what do we know about these scavengers?

657
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:33,960
他们的船肯定有什么弱点
Their ship has to have some kind of weakness.

658
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:36,720
乌乎拉 你观察到了什么
Uhura, what have you seen?

659
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:38,460
里面有很多船
Ships, a lot of them,

660
00:31:38,460 --> 00:31:41,130
来自象限的各个角落 它掳走船只
from across the quadrant. It appropriates them,

661
00:31:41,130 --> 00:31:42,400
窃取它们的能力
steals their functionality,

662
00:31:42,470 --> 00:31:43,770
然后为己所用
and bends that to its own needs.

663
00:31:43,770 --> 00:31:45,270
而且它的欲望永无止境
And its needs are bottomless.

664
00:31:45,270 --> 00:31:47,380
它只懂得不断吞噬 让自己变得更大
All it does is consume and make itself bigger.

665
00:31:47,380 --> 00:31:49,880
它变得越大 需要的就越多
The bigger it gets, the more it requires.

666
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:51,750
然后就会去吞噬下一个资源 就是
Then it moves on to devour the next resource, like...

667
00:31:51,810 --> 00:31:52,810
它永远不会停下
it will never stop,

668
00:31:52,950 --> 00:31:54,350
它永远不会满足
you know, it'll never have enough.

669
00:31:54,450 --> 00:31:57,190
没错 斯科提 你刚才已经找到了他们的弱点
Exactly. Scotty, you just found their weakness:

670
00:31:57,320 --> 00:31:59,820
极度过分的吞噬欲
their ravenous need to consume.

671
00:31:59,950 --> 00:32:01,720
无尽的贪欲
Bottomless greed.

672
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:02,960
我们可以利用这点来对抗它们
We can use that against them.

673
00:32:03,020 --> 00:32:03,850
该怎么做
How?

674
00:32:04,630 --> 00:32:06,500
这就要轮到你出场了
That's where you come in.

675
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:08,380
我需要你用奥登金充满等离子歧管
I need you to fill the plasma manifold

676
00:32:08,380 --> 00:32:10,160
直到溢出为止
until it's overflowing with aldentium.

677
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:11,340
不 不 歧管只是个没用的壳子
No-no, the-the manifold's a useless husk,

678
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:13,440
况且船上连一滴奥登金都没有
and we don't have a drop of aldentium on board.

679
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:16,200
我们只需要让它看起来像
We just need to make it look like we do.

680
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,200
随着奥登金衰变
As aldentium decays,

681
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,820
这个过程中会释放出很多反质子
it gives off lots of anti-protons.

682
00:32:18,820 --> 00:32:20,680
我可以用反质子来填充混合室
Well, I could flood the intermix chamber with anti-protons

683
00:32:20,770 --> 00:32:22,770
让我们的引擎看起来像是由奥登金驱动的
and make it look like our engines run on aldentium.

684
00:32:22,870 --> 00:32:25,210
它们会发现我们的踪迹 被我们的排气管吸引过来
They'll catch the scent and gravitate towards our tailpipe.

685
00:32:25,310 --> 00:32:27,450
我们要把法拉格特号
We are going to make the Farragut

686
00:32:27,550 --> 00:32:31,040
伪装成一场令拾荒者垂涎欲滴的盛宴
into a banquet that's impossible for these scavengers to resist, 

687
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:32,020
当它们来赴宴时
and when they come to dine,

688
00:32:32,150 --> 00:32:34,090
就该后悔得肠子都青了
we're going to make them regret it.

689
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:39,460
舰长已经下令了
The captain has given his orders.

690
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:49,030
我还是觉得这么叫怪怪的 维瑞尔还活着呢
I still feel funny being called that while V'Rel's alive.

691
00:32:49,140 --> 00:32:52,010
我保证一有机会就会尽快给你降职
I promise to demote you at the earliest opportunity.

692
00:32:53,710 --> 00:32:59,010
等等 所以在这些拾荒者尝试吃掉我们的时候 我们又该怎么办
Wait, so what exactly do we do after we get these scavengers to try and eat us?

693
00:32:59,010 --> 00:33:01,150
这就是这个计划有点疯狂的地方了
Here's where the plan gets a little crazy.

694
00:33:01,210 --> 00:33:03,560
什么这个计划有点疯狂的地方
This is where the plan gets crazy?

695
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:04,780
幸好你正坐着呢 查普尔护士
Glad you're sitting down, Nurse Chapel.

696
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,980
尤其是你 斯考特先生
You especially, Mr. Scott,

697
00:33:07,090 --> 00:33:09,060
你不会喜欢这个的
are not going to love it.

698
00:33:23,900 --> 00:33:25,200
拉安
La'An!

699
00:34:26,740 --> 00:34:29,020
警告 环境指标危险

700
00:34:46,490 --> 00:34:47,320
你还好吗
You all right?

701
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:48,080
还好
Yeah.

702
00:34:49,720 --> 00:34:52,060
它没有开枪
It... didn't shoot.

703
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,660
为什么它不杀了我
Why didn't it kill me?

704
00:35:09,740 --> 00:35:10,910
我们可能只有一分钟的时间
We may only have a minute.

705
00:35:10,910 --> 00:35:12,760
该怎么把这死东西从我的船上弄下来
How do we get this thing the hell off my ship?

706
00:35:12,760 --> 00:35:15,360
如果我们不能切断它 那么说服它们呢
Well, if we can't disconnect it, what if we convince them to?

707
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:17,240
-什么意思 -让它们自愿断开连接
- How do you mean? - Make them want to disconnect it.

708
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:19,350
让它们尝到点
Give them a taste of something...

709
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:20,750
难吃的东西
highly undesirable.

710
00:35:21,560 --> 00:35:22,840
我懂了 让它觉得反胃酸了
I see, stir up a little acid reflux?

711
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:24,020
是的
Yeah.

712
00:35:24,020 --> 00:35:25,740
重子粒子如何
What about, uh, baryon particles?

713
00:35:25,740 --> 00:35:27,190
那它们的燃料和美好的一天就都该完蛋了
That would ruin their fuel and their day.

714
00:35:27,290 --> 00:35:28,760
我们其中一个必须进入曲速引擎下面的
One of us would have to access the waste system

715
00:35:28,860 --> 00:35:30,100
废物处理系统
beneath the warp drive.

716
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:32,540
废物处理系统 好吧 你去吧
Waste system? All right, you do that.

717
00:35:34,340 --> 00:35:36,000
我得把燃料管道隔离
I have to isolate the fuel line.

718
00:35:37,540 --> 00:35:39,300
还有  拿一个超耦合器过来
And bring a hyper coupler.

719
00:35:40,110 --> 00:35:41,610
拉安
La'An

720
00:35:41,670 --> 00:35:44,170
小心点 还有一个外星人活着
Be careful, that other alien's still out there.

721
00:35:59,260 --> 00:36:01,830
女士们 上次我干这种话
Ladies, I haven't done this

722
00:36:01,830 --> 00:36:04,500
还是给死人乐队打杂的时候呢
since I was a roadie for the Dead.

723
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:07,570
你这个种族还可以和死人交流吗
Your species can communicate with dead people?

724
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:09,440
你好
Hello?

725
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:10,940
是的 是的
Ah, ah, yes, yes.

726
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:13,780
上尉 找你的
Uh, uh, Lieutenant, it's for you.

727
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:18,920
喂
Hello?

728
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:20,360
右舷推进器已经准备好了
Starboard thrusters are ready.

729
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:22,420
左舷推进器也准备就绪
Port thrusters standing by.

730
00:36:24,180 --> 00:36:27,050
好吧 艾丽卡 小心别坠机
Okay, Erica, don't crash.

731
00:36:36,080 --> 00:36:37,760
拾荒者星舰已脱离曲速
The scavenger vessel has dropped out of warp.

732
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:40,360
反质子 正在反着质子
Anti-protons... anti-protoning?

733
00:36:40,430 --> 00:36:42,870
我们现在已经美味到极限了
We're as juicy a target as I can make us.

734
00:36:42,930 --> 00:36:44,700
红色警报 各岗位准备
Red alert. All stations prepare for...

735
00:36:46,840 --> 00:36:49,210
好吧 准备被吃
...well, for that.

736
00:36:49,380 --> 00:36:50,820
脉冲引擎准备
Ready impulse engines.

737
00:36:50,820 --> 00:36:51,500
已就绪
Standing by.

738
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:53,210
她掌舵过多少次
How many times has she helmed?

739
00:36:53,210 --> 00:36:54,910
两次 包括这次
Twice, including now.

740
00:36:56,260 --> 00:36:57,430
脉冲全速 乌乎拉
Full impulse, Uhura.

741
00:37:13,580 --> 00:37:14,800
斯考提 轮到你了
Scotty, your turn.

742
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:15,670
如果你坚持的话
If you insist.

743
00:37:15,670 --> 00:37:16,810
我坚持 斯考特先生
I do, Mr. Scott.

744
00:37:16,900 --> 00:37:19,000
听我口令分离
Detach at my mark.

745
00:37:23,140 --> 00:37:24,080
分离
Mark.

746
00:37:32,200 --> 00:37:33,600
史波克
Spock?

747
00:37:34,690 --> 00:37:37,120
贪吃蛇咬到自己尾巴了 舰长
The sehlat has eaten its tail, Captain.

748
00:37:37,120 --> 00:37:39,320
拾荒者星舰已被瘫痪
The scavenger ship has been disabled.

749
00:37:40,540 --> 00:37:43,600
乌乎拉 尽快找到进取号
Uhura, get us line of sight to the Enterprise as quickly as you can.

750
00:37:46,460 --> 00:37:48,000
接收到信号传输
Incoming transmission.

751
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:50,340
是法拉格特号 仅音频
It's the Farragut, audio only.

752
00:37:50,340 --> 00:37:51,670
进取号 能收到吗
Enterprise, do you read?

753
00:37:51,670 --> 00:37:53,200
可算来了啊 少尉
Took you long enough, Ensign.

754
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:54,800
我也很高兴听到你的声音
Good to hear your voice, too.

755
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:57,720
我们受损严重 但是我们已经瘫痪了拾荒者星舰
We're pretty banged up, but we disabled the scavenger ship.

756
00:37:57,720 --> 00:37:59,480
告诉她这只是暂时的
Tell her it's just temporary.

757
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:00,520
能持续多久
How temporary?

758
00:38:00,520 --> 00:38:02,480
不清楚 但这是你们的机会
No idea, but this is your chance.

759
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:03,920
越狱的机会
For a jailbreak.

760
00:38:10,890 --> 00:38:12,660
左 右舷推进器
Port and starboard thrusters,

761
00:38:12,660 --> 00:38:14,430
百分之十动力
give me ten percent.

762
00:38:16,130 --> 00:38:18,340
我们得关闭推进器 我们还没脱离束缚
we got to kill those thrusters. We are not off-leash.

763
00:38:20,860 --> 00:38:22,600
舰长 找到燃料线路了吗
Captain, any luck finding the fuel line?

764
00:38:22,600 --> 00:38:25,000
我有一个相当可靠的猜测
I've got a pretty solid guess.

765
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:30,510
把那个连接器递给我
Hand me that connector?

766
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:33,980
你最好后退一步
And you might want to take a step back.

767
00:38:34,880 --> 00:38:37,550
如果爆炸 整个工程部船体都会被炸掉
If it explodes, it will take out the entire engineering hull.

768
00:38:37,550 --> 00:38:38,850
多退几步吧
A big step, then?

769
00:38:47,900 --> 00:38:50,700
重子粒子正在进入氘粒子流
Baryon particles are entering the deuterium stream.

770
00:38:50,700 --> 00:38:54,580
混合物 正在失去稳定
The mixture is... destabilizing.

771
00:38:54,580 --> 00:38:55,700
趁我们还没被这东西吸走
Let's get the hell out of here

772
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:57,100
赶紧跑路吧
before we get sucked out with this thing.

773
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:07,060
等等
Wait.

774
00:39:07,060 --> 00:39:08,590
紧急系统正在重启
Emergency systems are rebooting.

775
00:39:09,030 --> 00:39:10,750
舰长做到了 这些脐带正在脱离
Captain did it. The umbilical's detached.

776
00:39:10,750 --> 00:39:12,250
左 右舷推进器
Port and starboard thrusters,

777
00:39:12,250 --> 00:39:13,320
百分之五十
50%.

778
00:39:14,520 --> 00:39:15,900
右舷推进器减缓点
Ease off starboard thrusters. Whoa.

779
00:39:15,900 --> 00:39:18,320
别减这么多 给我百分之三十
N-Not that easy. Give me 30%.

780
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:20,320
百分之五十 现在等下
50%. Now wait.

781
00:39:20,320 --> 00:39:21,560
五十 八十
50, 80.

782
00:39:21,560 --> 00:39:22,860
切断右舷推进器
Cut starboard thrusters.

783
00:39:25,100 --> 00:39:27,500
我也不想说风凉话 但是你要撞墙
Hate to backseat-drive, but you're hitting the wall.

784
00:39:27,570 --> 00:39:28,900
左舷推进器全速
Full port thrusters.

785
00:39:29,030 --> 00:39:30,870
推进器控制无响应
Thruster controls aren't responding.

786
00:39:30,970 --> 00:39:32,440
这要完蛋了
That's real bad.

787
00:39:32,540 --> 00:39:33,740
等等 我有个想法
Wait, I have an idea.

788
00:39:33,870 --> 00:39:35,770
洗耳恭听
I'm all ears.

789
00:39:35,870 --> 00:39:38,170
中校?
Commander?

790
00:39:39,280 --> 00:39:41,050
中校?
Commander?

791
00:40:03,670 --> 00:40:07,170
好 右舷推进器动力20%
Yes! Starboard thrusters to 20%.

792
00:40:08,600 --> 00:40:10,110
保持平衡
Keep us even.

793
00:40:12,460 --> 00:40:13,480
舰长
Captain.

794
00:40:14,820 --> 00:40:16,160
是拾荒者
The scavenger.

795
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:21,920
拾荒者星舰的系统正在恢复运行
The scavenger vessel's systems are coming back on line.

796
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:23,560
他们正在瞄准进取号
They are targeting Enterprise.

797
00:40:23,660 --> 00:40:24,800
相位炮锁定
Lock phasers.

798
00:40:24,890 --> 00:40:26,660
呃
Uh...

799
00:40:26,760 --> 00:40:27,900
舰长 我们的武器无法
Sir, the grapplers have proven

800
00:40:27,990 --> 00:40:29,730
有效应对那些抓钩
to be resistant to our weapons.

801
00:40:29,830 --> 00:40:31,970
好吧 史波克
Okay, Spock.

802
00:40:32,060 --> 00:40:33,660
你有什么主意吗
What do you got?

803
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:30,250
史波克先生 扫描残骸中的生命信号
Mr. Spock, scan the debris for life signs.

804
00:41:35,690 --> 00:41:38,160
近7000个生命信号
Approximately 7,000 life signs,

805
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:40,340
在迅速减少
but they are dwindling quickly.

806
00:41:40,340 --> 00:41:42,030
我们能把生还者传送到船上吗
Can we beam survivors aboard?

807
00:41:44,340 --> 00:41:45,740
我们有心无力
Not even if we wanted to.

808
00:41:45,740 --> 00:41:48,270
残骸的碎片会影响传送器 无法锁定
There's too much debris to get a transporter lock.

809
00:41:55,110 --> 00:41:56,980
舰长
Captain?

810
00:41:56,980 --> 00:41:58,380
那些生命信号
The life signs.

811
00:41:58,480 --> 00:42:00,780
是的 史波克先生
Yes, Mr. Spock?

812
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:28,910
那些生命信号全都是人类
The life signs are all human.

813
00:42:40,790 --> 00:42:42,990
船体上的标记
The markings on the hull.

814
00:42:44,100 --> 00:42:45,760
我们能看得更清楚一点吗
Can you get us a clearer image?

815
00:42:46,560 --> 00:42:47,760
好的
Aye.

816
00:42:57,940 --> 00:43:01,180
我在历史数据库里找到了这个
I found this in our historical database.

817
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:05,450
21世纪中期
In the mid-21st century,

818
00:43:05,450 --> 00:43:07,520
在与瓦肯人的第一次接触之前
before first contact with the Vulcans,

819
00:43:07,520 --> 00:43:09,430
有一群科学家 他们认为
a group of scientists believed

820
00:43:09,430 --> 00:43:13,500
岌岌可危的地球环境
that Earth's environmental crisis was too severe

821
00:43:13,500 --> 00:43:16,790
没有复原的可能 所以他们建造了一艘飞船
to recover from, so they built a ship.

822
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:19,100
他们希望这艘船能让人类文明
They hoped it would carry humanity

823
00:43:19,100 --> 00:43:21,730
在其他世界中继续生根发芽
to civilizations in other worlds.

824
00:43:21,730 --> 00:43:24,100
但事与愿违
But it failed.

825
00:43:24,170 --> 00:43:26,470
这艘船消失了
The ship disappeared.

826
00:43:27,370 --> 00:43:29,270
全体船员
The entire crew,

827
00:43:29,270 --> 00:43:32,140
他们的家人 都消失了
their families, gone.

828
00:43:35,680 --> 00:43:37,850
此后音讯全无
Never heard from again.

829
00:43:38,720 --> 00:43:41,790
我还记得这艘船发射升空时的事
I remember when it launched.

830
00:43:41,790 --> 00:43:46,020
那时我们还没有发明曲速引擎
We-we hadn't yet invented warp drive.

831
00:43:46,970 --> 00:43:51,130
第三次世界大战才堪堪结束
We'd barely put out the fires of the Third World War.

832
00:43:51,130 --> 00:43:54,830
熬过战争的国家不多 其中一个
One of the few nations left standing

833
00:43:54,830 --> 00:43:58,800
在他们残存的航天计划中挑选
sifted through the ashes of their space program,

834
00:43:58,800 --> 00:44:02,160
走遍全世界招募了一批船员
scoured the world for a crew.

835
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:03,500
可以说
You might say...

836
00:44:05,170 --> 00:44:08,010
那是当年最出类拔萃的一批人
...they were the best of us,

837
00:44:08,010 --> 00:44:10,380
最为乐观积极
the most optimistic,

838
00:44:10,840 --> 00:44:13,500
他们拼尽全力寻找
searching for a way to carry on

839
00:44:13,500 --> 00:44:15,760
延续文明之火的方式
the flame of life.

840
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:17,540
那么多船员
All those people.

841
00:44:18,680 --> 00:44:20,460
7000条生命
7,000 souls.

842
00:44:20,460 --> 00:44:23,360
他们是初始船员们的后人
The descendants of the original inhabitants.

843
00:44:23,360 --> 00:44:25,030
到底出了什么差错
So what went wrong?

844
00:44:27,580 --> 00:44:29,440
他们为什么会从那样一批优秀的船员变成
How did they go from that to...

845
00:44:31,200 --> 00:44:33,170
现在这个样子
...whatever it is they became?

846
00:44:43,750 --> 00:44:45,350
请进
Come in.

847
00:44:48,050 --> 00:44:49,180
啊
Ah...

848
00:44:49,290 --> 00:44:50,690
只是想当面告诉你
Just wanted to let you know in person,

849
00:44:50,760 --> 00:44:52,460
姆'本加医生说维瑞尔舰长
Dr. M'Benga says that Captain V'Rel is going

850
00:44:52,560 --> 00:44:54,030
之后会完全康复的
to make a complete recovery.

851
00:44:54,130 --> 00:44:56,400
我们会把法拉格特号拖回船坞
We'll tow Farragut back to spacedock.

852
00:44:56,490 --> 00:44:57,730
你只需要
Then you only have

853
00:44:57,860 --> 00:44:59,360
再撑一会儿就好
to hold the fort down a little while longer.

854
00:44:59,460 --> 00:45:02,200
拖回去一艘没了曲速舱的船
I'm imagining the look on Admiral April's face

855
00:45:02,300 --> 00:45:04,800
我几乎都能想象到艾普里尔上将的表情了
when he sees us pull in with no nacelles.

856
00:45:04,900 --> 00:45:07,180
他喜欢毕宿五威士忌
He likes Aldebaran whiskey.

857
00:45:07,680 --> 00:45:09,040
备好一瓶以备不时之需
Maybe have a bottle ready.

858
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:11,380
可能你会觉得很难受 但你确实做出了正确的决定
You know, it might not feel like it, but you made the right call.

859
00:45:11,480 --> 00:45:13,180
我们遭到了攻击
We were under attack.

860
00:45:13,280 --> 00:45:16,720
你拯救了几百条生命 法拉格特号上的和进取号上的
You saved hundreds of lives, both here and on Enterprise.

861
00:45:16,820 --> 00:45:18,820
未知船只
Number of...

862
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:22,290
上的预估伤亡人数是
estimated human casualties on unknown vessel...

863
00:45:23,820 --> 00:45:25,620
七千
...7,000.

864
00:45:28,720 --> 00:45:30,060
我可以坐下吗
Well, may I?

865
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:32,230
请坐
Please.

866
00:45:39,240 --> 00:45:40,710
你知道 我刚晋升
You know, when, uh...

867
00:45:40,710 --> 00:45:42,880
为大副的时候
when I got bumped up to first officer,

868
00:45:42,940 --> 00:45:44,670
我记得我经常怀疑鲍勃
I remember second-guessing Bob--

869
00:45:44,780 --> 00:45:47,320
就是艾普里尔上将
uh, Admiral April-- a lot.

870
00:45:47,410 --> 00:45:49,180
难道他没有为此纠正你的想法吗
Did he ever straighten you out?

871
00:45:49,180 --> 00:45:50,019
没有
No.

872
00:45:50,019 --> 00:45:52,420
他给了我一个深刻的教训
He let me learn a very hard lesson.

873
00:45:53,680 --> 00:45:55,090
重大的决定背后需要肩负的责任
The big decisions-- they seem so simple

874
00:45:55,090 --> 00:45:57,160
只有在别人身上才看起来轻松
when someone else has to live with the consequences,

875
00:45:57,290 --> 00:45:59,960
但当你坐在舰长的位置上 作出的每一个决定
but the choices you make in that chair...

876
00:46:00,960 --> 00:46:02,960
都是你需要肩负的责任
...they are yours to make...

877
00:46:04,440 --> 00:46:06,170
其后果
...and what comes after...

878
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:09,670
也是你必须承担的
...that is yours to live with.

879
00:46:10,380 --> 00:46:13,340
有一些决定会让你悔恨终生
Some decisions you will regret for the rest of your life,

880
00:46:13,340 --> 00:46:14,840
但你仍然不得不去做
but you still have to make them.

881
00:46:14,840 --> 00:46:16,240
那些人都是人类
They were human beings.

882
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:20,760
为什么我会觉得更难受了
Why does that make it feel so much worse?

883
00:46:20,760 --> 00:46:21,850
我能说的只有
All I can say is...

884
00:46:23,059 --> 00:46:25,450
同情你的敌人是工作时的必经之途
...having empathy for your adversary is part of the job.

885
00:46:25,450 --> 00:46:27,190
但我没有
But I didn't.

886
00:46:28,180 --> 00:46:30,320
我没想过他们会是人类
I didn't think of them as people...

887
00:46:30,320 --> 00:46:32,060
从头到尾
at all.

888
00:46:33,090 --> 00:46:34,460
然后一切都无法挽回了
Until it was too late.

889
00:46:34,460 --> 00:46:36,500
也许这正是我们应当反思的
Well, maybe that's the lesson.

890
00:46:37,760 --> 00:46:39,020
同情是不看对象的
Empathy isn't conditional.

891
00:46:39,020 --> 00:46:40,280
有就是有 没有就是没有
It's either given or it isn't.

892
00:46:40,280 --> 00:46:43,040
他们肯定看见了我们的模样
They... clearly saw us,

893
00:46:43,720 --> 00:46:46,000
要么他们没有认出我们 要么他们不在乎
and either they didn't recognize us or they didn't care.

894
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:47,360
无论过去两百年
Whatever journey they had been through

895
00:46:47,360 --> 00:46:48,800
发生了什么 他们已经不是当初的那批船员了
the last 200 years, it broke them.

896
00:46:48,800 --> 00:46:49,740
他们离开地球的时候
When they left Earth...

897
00:46:51,920 --> 00:46:54,780
是全人类中最优秀的
...they were the best humanity had to offer.

898
00:46:54,780 --> 00:46:57,020
他们过去并不是怪物
They weren't monsters.

899
00:46:59,020 --> 00:47:01,520
我们在同样的情况下也会变成那样吗
Is that what we would become in the same circumstances?

900
00:47:01,520 --> 00:47:03,290
我想我们不会的
I'd like to believe we wouldn't.

901
00:47:03,660 --> 00:47:04,460
为什么
Why not?

902
00:47:04,460 --> 00:47:06,110
因为我们对他们怀有同情
Because of how you're feeling right now.

903
00:47:06,110 --> 00:47:07,360
因为下一次你作为舰长下达指令的时候
Because the next time you're in that chair,

904
00:47:07,360 --> 00:47:09,200
你会想起我们与我们的敌人
you will remember we are often not that different

905
00:47:09,290 --> 00:47:11,460
并没有那么不同
from our enemy.

906
00:47:13,190 --> 00:47:15,430
这种认识
And that knowledge,

907
00:47:15,430 --> 00:47:17,300
从现在起
from this moment on,

908
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:19,540
会永远指引着你
will continue to guide you.

909
00:47:28,510 --> 00:47:31,610
晚安 柯克舰长
Good night, Captain Kirk.

